Here's how to do it using `Window` lifecycle events and `Preferences`:

**1. Create a custom `Window` subclass:**

```csharp
public class AppWindow : Window
{
    public AppWindow(Page page) : base(page) { }

    protected override void OnStopped()
    {
        base.OnStopped();
        if (Page is AppShell shell)
        {
            var vm = GetNoteViewModel(shell);
            if (vm != null)
                Preferences.Set("draft_text", vm.DraftText);
        }
    }

    protected override void OnResumed()
    {
        base.OnResumed();
        if (Page is AppShell shell)
        {
            var vm = GetNoteViewModel(shell);
            if (vm != null)
                vm.DraftText = Preferences.Get("draft_text", string.Empty);
        }
    }

    protected override void OnDestroying()
    {
        base.OnDestroying();
        // Android back-button can skip Stopped entirely
        if (Page is AppShell shell)
        {
            var vm = GetNoteViewModel(shell);
            if (vm != null)
                Preferences.Set("draft_text", vm.DraftText);
        }
    }

    private NoteViewModel? GetNoteViewModel(AppShell shell)
        => (shell.CurrentPage?.BindingContext) as NoteViewModel;
}
```

**2. Return it from `App.CreateWindow`:**

```csharp
public partial class App : Application
{
    protected override Window CreateWindow(IActivationState? activationState)
        => new AppWindow(new AppShell());
}
```

**Key points:**

- **`OnStopped`** fires when the app is fully backgrounded — save here.
- **`OnResumed`** fires when returning from background — restore here.
- **`OnDestroying`** also saves because Android's back button can skip `Stopped` and go straight to `Destroying`.
- Use `Preferences` for small values like draft text — it's fast enough to avoid ANR timeouts on Android (~5s limit).
- **Don't use `OnDeactivated`** for saving — it fires for transient focus loss (notification shade, split-screen) and the app may never actually background.
- `OnResumed` does **not** fire on first launch (sequence is `Created` → `Activated`), so load any persisted draft in your page/viewmodel constructor as well.
